.TH IFNH 1 "" "ifnh" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ifnh \- a tiny, fast, developer-controlled agentic coding harness
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ifnh
.RB [ global\-flags ]
.RI [ subcommand
.RI [ args ...]]
.br
.B ifnh \-p
.I prompt
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ifnh
runs a coding agent in your terminal against a model provider of your choice.
With no subcommand it starts an interactive session in the current directory.
Behaviour that can be expressed as JSON or Markdown (configuration, skills,
commands, instructions) is read from disk at run time; project state lives in
.B .ifnh/
and is never created outside the directory you run it in.
.PP
Flags are kebab-case. Unknown flags are errors, not ignored values.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B (none)
Start an interactive session.
.TP
.B init
Create a
.B .ifnh/
project skeleton. Never overwrites existing files.
.TP
.B config validate | explain \fIkey\fR | get \fIkey\fR | set \fIkey value\fR | edit | path | schema
Inspect and change configuration.
.B set
and
.B edit
write one file and validate before writing;
.B set
takes
.B \-\-project
(default) or
.BR \-\-global .
.TP
.B sessions \fR[\fBlist\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
List recorded sessions.
.TP
.B resume \fIsession\-id\fR
Resume a previous session.
.TP
.B fork \fIsession\-id\fR
Branch a session into a new one.
.B fork diff \fIa b\fR
compares two sessions.
.TP
.B cleanup
Enforce retention; list and remove worktrees.
.TP
.B ask \fR[\fIprompt\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-yes\fR | \fB\-\-deny\-all\fR | \fB\-\-policy\fR \fIask|allow|deny\fR] [\fB\-p\fR \fIprompt\fR] [\fB\-\-image\fR \fIpath\fR]...
Run one headless turn. The prompt is an argument, or read from standard input
when omitted or
.BR \- .
.B \-\-json
prints NDJSON events and nothing else.
.B \-\-yes
approves every permission ask once;
.B \-\-deny\-all
denies every ask; they and
.B \-\-policy
are mutually exclusive. Without them, asks are answered on the terminal.
.B \-\-image
attaches a png, jpg, gif or webp (at most 5 MiB), up to eight times.
.TP
.B doctor
Check environment health. Exits 1 if a check fails.
.TP
.B serve \fR[\fB\-\-framing\fR \fIndjson|content\-length\fR]
Speak JSON-RPC 2.0 (ACP) over standard input and output.
.TP
.B memory list \fR[\fB\-\-scope\fR \fIproject|user\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
.TQ
.B memory purge \fR[\fB\-\-scope\fR \fIproject|user\fR] [\fB\-\-yes\fR]
List or purge stored memory. Both report that memory is off while
.B memory.adapter
is
.BR none .
.TP
.B debug\-bundle \fR[\fB\-\-out\fR \fIpath\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Write a redacted JSON bundle for bug reports.
.TP
.B session export \fIid\fR [\fB\-\-out\fR \fIpath\fR|\fB\-\fR]
Write a session as redacted NDJSON.
.TP
.B replay \fIfile\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Print an exported session offline.
.TP
.B completions \fIbash|zsh|fish\fR
Print a shell completion script to standard output. For example:
.RS
.nf
ifnh completions bash > ~/.local/share/bash\-completion/completions/ifnh
ifnh completions zsh > ~/.local/share/zsh/site\-functions/_ifnh
ifnh completions fish > ~/.config/fish/completions/ifnh.fish
.fi
.RE
.TP
.B update
Disabled. IFNH never replaces its own binary; it prints how to upgrade and
exits 1. Package managers own upgrades and removal.
.TP
.B help
Show the built-in help.
.TP
.B version \fR[\fB\-\-verbose\fR]
Print the version. With
.BR \-\-verbose ,
also print the commit, target and build mode.
.SH GLOBAL FLAGS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable output.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable color.
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-level " level"
One of
.BR err ,
.BR info ,
.B debug
or
.BR trace .
.TP
.BI \-\-profile " name"
Apply
.BI profiles. name
from configuration.
.TP
.BI \-\-trace " path"
Write a redacted NDJSON wire log (or set
.BR IFNH_TRACE_LOG ).
.TP
.BI \-\-model " id\fR, " \-\-provider " name\fR, " \-\-base\-url " url\fR, " \-\-temperature " n"
.TQ
.BI \-\-max\-output\-tokens " n\fR, " \-\-context\-tokens " n\fR, " \-\-permission\-mode " mode"
.TQ
.B \-\-no\-footer
Per-key configuration overrides, applied after
.B \-\-profile
as the highest-precedence layer.
.TP
.BI \-p " prompt"
Headless one-shot prompt; the same as
.B ifnh ask \-p
.IR prompt .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ifnh
.TQ
.I ~/.config/ifnh
User configuration (\fIconfig.json\fR), user skills and stored API keys. The first is used when
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is set, otherwise the second. The same on Linux and macOS.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/ifnh
Logs and transient state.
.TP
.I .ifnh/
Project configuration, instructions, skills, commands, plans and sessions. Package
managers and the installer never create, modify or remove it.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base of the user configuration directory.
.TP
.BI IFNH_ SECTION __ KEY
Override a configuration key, for example
.BR IFNH_PERMISSIONS__DEFAULT_MODE=auto .
.TP
.B IFNH_TRACE_LOG
Path of the redacted wire log (same as
.BR \-\-trace ).
.TP
.BR ANTHROPIC_API_KEY ", " OPENAI_API_KEY ", " GEMINI_API_KEY
Provider keys, when not stored in the user configuration directory.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Failure: provider or tool error that ended the turn, or a failed check.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error: unknown flag, bad or missing value, missing prompt.
.TP
.B 3
Denied: a tool call was denied during the turn (\fBask\fR).
.TP
.B 4
Budget: \fBagents.budget_usd\fR was already spent (\fBask\fR).
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted.
.SH SEE ALSO
Full guide: docs/USAGE.md in the source repository, or
.B ifnh help
for the built-in summary. Release artifacts and their verification are described
in the section "Release artifacts" of that guide.
